# Open Brain Email History Import
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# Then: export $(cat .env | xargs)

# Supabase (from your Open Brain setup — Credential Tracker)
SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key-here

# OpenRouter (for embedding generation and metadata extraction)
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-your-key-here

# Optional: Custom ingest endpoint (use with --ingest-endpoint flag)
# INGEST_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co/functions/v1/ingest-thought
# INGEST_KEY=your-ingest-key-here

# --- Self-hosted stack (OB1/docker/docker-compose.scheduled.yml) -------------
# openbrain-gmail-pull and openbrain-gmail-prune load this file as an OPTIONAL
# env_file: the plane renders without it, but the chain does no work until it
# holds real values (and the OAuth files under OB1/secrets/google/ exist).
# In the stack the "Supabase" pair above points at the local PostgREST proxy:
#   SUPABASE_URL=http://openbrain-rest:80
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<any non-empty value; Caddy strips it>
# and OPENROUTER_API_KEY is sent only as the bearer to the LOCAL embed server
# (pull-gmail.ts refuses a live run while it is empty; nothing goes to OpenRouter).
#
# Local inference (pull-gmail.ts). Shown values are the in-code defaults.
# LOCAL_LLM_BASE=http://llama-cpp:8080/v1
# LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=qwen36-27b:nothink
# LOCAL_EMBED_BASE=http://llama-cpp-embed:8080/v1
# LOCAL_EMBED_MODEL=bge-m3
#
# Short-term retention (pull-gmail.ts + prune-short-term.ts; in-code defaults).
# BRAIN_SHORT_TERM_RETENTION_DAYS=90
# BRAIN_SHORT_TERM_LABEL=brain/keep-short-term
#
# Wiki recompile after a prune (prune-short-term.ts). The URL defaults to the
# wiki profile's service; MCP_ACCESS_KEY must equal MCP_ACCESS_KEY in
# OB1/docker/.env, and while it is empty the prune skips the recompile.
# WIKI_RECOMPILE_URL=http://openbrain-wiki:8000/recompile
# MCP_ACCESS_KEY=
